title: "SE+ Shoreline Extractor: lidar-constrained shoreline extraction for mixed marsh and non-marsh coasts (ArcGIS Pro toolbox)"
type: software
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23301832"
authors:
  - family-names: "Dwira"
    given-names: "Curtis Amo"
    affiliation: "Louisiana State University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-3565-6338"
repository-code: "https://github.com/amodwira/SHORELINE-EXTRACTOR-SE--ARCGIS_PRO-"
keywords:
  - shoreline extraction
  - satellite-derived shoreline
  - MNDWI
  - lidar
  - salt marsh
  - coastal Louisiana
  - Sentinel-2
  - ArcGIS Pro
abstract: >-
  An ArcGIS Pro Python toolbox that extracts shorelines from multispectral
  imagery (MNDWI with Otsu thresholding) and, optionally, constrains the
  land-water decision with a bare-earth lidar DEM referenced to Mean High
  Water. Vegetated ground near MHW is identified as marsh (NDVI), shoreline
  segments are labelled marsh or non-marsh, and the non-marsh shoreline and
  the marsh shoreline are delivered as separate layers together with a
  segmentation map (open water, inland water, land, marsh).
